---
import { cta, launchPlan } from '../../lib/site';
// Considered Composite; not used because the opening is one fixed decision and
// one worked example, not a recursive content tree.
---
<!-- story: docs/stories/homepage-caterer-fixes.story.md -->
<section class="container-page py-8 sm:py-12" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
  <div class="hero-layout">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-deep">Back-of-house software for independent caterers, meal-prep kitchens, and restaurants that cater</p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading" class="anim-enter mt-4 text-display font-semibold">Cost it, buy it, prep it, pack it.</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[54ch] text-base text-ink-soft sm:text-lede">Use your recipes, current prices and guest count to check food cost and build the shopping, prep and pack lists. Change the count once; the lists change with it.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold">First dish: about fifteen minutes. Bring its recipe and ingredient prices.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2">
        <a href={cta.href} target={cta.target} rel={cta.rel} aria-label={cta.ariaLabel} class="btn-primary">{cta.label}</a>
        <a href="#demo" class="btn-quiet">Watch the 2:53 product tour <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft"><strong>{launchPlan.trialDays} days free</strong>, then {launchPlan.displayPrice} {launchPlan.unit}, {launchPlan.crew}. Card up front, charged $0 today. Nothing to install.</p>
      <a href="/pricing#launch-terms" class="mt-1 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-sm font-semibold text-green-deep underline underline-offset-4">Read the launch terms</a>
    </div>
    <figure class="quote-proof" aria-labelledby="quote-proof-title">
      <figcaption id="quote-proof-title" class="font-semibold">A sample wedding, checked before you quote</figcaption>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">180 guests × $68 = $12,240 revenue</p>
      <dl class="quote-values">
        <div><dt>Food per guest</dt><dd>$26.93</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Food-cost share</dt><dd>39.6%</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Example food-cost target</dt><dd>30%</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-green-deep">$89.78 per guest to meet a 30% food-cost target.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">Food only: packaging, rentals, staff and anything you cook over the guarantee sit outside it.</p>
      <details class="mt-4 border-t border-hairline pt-2">
        <summary class="min-h-11 cursor-pointer py-3 font-semibold text-green-deep">Inspect the pricing panel</summary>
        <a href="/proof/hero-pricing.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="block py-3" aria-label="Open the full-size pricing panel in a new tab">
          <img src="/proof/hero-pricing.png" alt="Food-cost target panel: 39.6% food cost against a 30% target. Charge at least $89.78 per guest to meet it; food-only exclusions are shown." width="1284" height="366" decoding="async" class="h-auto w-full" />
          <span class="mt-2 block text-sm font-semibold underline">Open full-size panel (new tab)</span>
        </a>
      </details>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">What you do about the gap is your call: swap a protein, drop a dish, raise the price, or take the job at that margin knowing it.</p>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <aside class="first-dish" aria-labelledby="first-dish-title" data-first-dish-preparation>
    <div>
      <h2 id="first-dish-title" class="text-h3 font-semibold">Try one dish before moving the kitchen.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch]">Have its recipe and ingredient prices ready, as invoices or price sheets. Upload them, confirm what CostCook read, and type anything missing. Allow about fifteen minutes for the first dish. A full menu needs its other dishes entered too.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Cancel before day {launchPlan.trialDays + 1} from Settings → Billing. No call required.</p>
      <a href="/onboarding" class="btn-quiet mt-3">See what setup takes</a>
    </div>
  </aside>
</section>
<style>
.hero-layout { display:grid; gap:2rem; align-items:start; }
.quote-proof { padding:1.25rem; background:var(--color-paper); border:1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule); }
.quote-values { margin-top:1rem; }
.quote-values div { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; padding-block:.65rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-hairline); }
.quote-values dt { color:var(--color-ink-soft); }
.quote-values dd { font-weight:700; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
.first-dish { display:grid; gap:1.25rem; margin-top:2rem; padding-block:1.5rem; border-block:1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule); }
@media(min-width:64rem) { .hero-layout { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:3rem; } .first-dish { grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr; gap:3rem; } }
</style>
